            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "For multiple daily users, higher body weights, serious mileage or a fifteen-year ownership horizon, yes. For one person walking or running an hour a day, the extra money buys durability margin you will not consume. The steepest value gain is between $500 and $1,000; the shallowest is between $2,500 and $4,000.",
          },
        },
